Write a function `count_lucky_triples` that takes a list of integers and returns the number of lucky triples in the list. A lucky triple is defined as three elements at indices i, j, k (i < j < k) such that the element at index j is a multiple of the element at index i, and the element at index k is a multiple of the element at index j. The function should return 0 for lists with fewer than three elements. The expected time complexity is O(n^2) where n is the length of the list.

---TEST---
